---
layout: null
permalink: /posts.json
---
{%- comment -%}
  Every post, rendered, for the blog viewer at the foot of the hub
  (dataterminals.github.io — blog.js there). The hub reads this rather than
  scraping the post pages, and `html` is each post's body exactly as its own
  page carries it: posts are built before pages, so by the time Jekyll gets to
  this file every post is already HTML — kramdown's output, Rouge's highlighting,
  every Liquid tag resolved — with no layout around it.

  Newest first, the order site.posts keeps; the hub sorts it both ways itself.
  `date` is the machine-readable one it sorts on; `label` is the date as the
  blog prints it, so the hub never formats one and can't land a post stamped
  at midnight UTC on the previous day west of Greenwich.

  Adding a field is safe; renaming one breaks the viewer until blog.js is told.
{%- endcomment -%}
{
  "posts": [
    {%- for post in site.posts %}
    {
      "title": {{ post.title | jsonify }},
      "date": {{ post.date | date_to_xmlschema | jsonify }},
      "label": {{ post.date | date: "%b %-d, %Y" | jsonify }},
      "url": {{ post.url | absolute_url | jsonify }},
      "html": {{ post.content | jsonify }}
    }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
